 "text": "Hi! How' life treating you? About one litre per hour is a good rule of thumb, more in heat and less at altitude where the air is thinner. Pick a drink you like, like a lemon orange or fruit soup, and take a little at a time. A bar of chocolate or some energy gel is handy if you grab you. And don't drink right before you stop, keep it going. Most people can a little, but some can't handle much at all. Better to check with your doctor or a coach before you train hard.",
